 " with plots, eigenmode visualizations, parameter sweeps, and interactive \
controls."
}], "ChatOutput",
 TaggingRules-><|
  "CellToStringData" -> 
   "/create_nb\n# Rigorous OPF Verification Notebook\n\n## Scientific status \
and scope\n\nThis notebook develops the proposed Ontological Physics \
Framework as a **formal symbolic model** and organizes all results into \
clearly separated layers:\n\n1. **Definitions and axioms**\n2. **Derived \
equations**\n3. **Internal consistency and proof obligations**\n4. **Spectral \
and stability analysis**\n5. **Measurement mappings and observable \
constructions**\n6. **Numerical experiments and convergence studies**\n7. \
**Interpretive remarks, explicitly separated from formal results**\n\nNo \
claim in this notebook is treated as established physical law unless it is \
derived internally from the stated assumptions.\n\n---\n\n## Notebook \
conventions\n\n```wl\nClearAll[\"Global`*\"];\n$HistoryLength = 0;\n```\n\n\
This notebook uses exact and symbolic computation whenever possible. \
Numerical computation is introduced only when a closed form is unavailable.\n\
\nA utility for consistent section banners:\n\n```wl\n\
ClearAll[sectionBanner];\nsectionBanner[text_String] := Style[text, 16, Bold, \
RGBColor[0.1, 0.2, 0.5]];\n```\n\nA utility for reporting tests:\n\n```wl\n\
ClearAll[reportTest];\nreportTest[name_String, expr_] := Association[\n   \
\"Name\" -> name,\n   \"Result\" -> Quiet@Check[expr, $Failed]\n];\n```\n\n\
---\n\n# 1. Formal statement of the framework\n\n## 1.1 Layer L0: nothingness \
geometry\n\nWe formalize the geometric substrate as a sphere together with a \
boundary-duality marker carrying the two special labels $0$ and $\\infty$.\n\n\
```wl\nClearAll[layer0, boundaryDuality, temporalMode, substrate];\n\nlayer0 \
= <|\n   \"Geometry\" -> Sphere[],\n   \"BoundaryDuality\" -> <|\"Vertices\" \
-> {0, Infinity}|>,\n   \"TemporalMode\" -> \"Timeless\",\n   \"Substrate\" \
-> \"EmptySpacetime\"\n|>;\n\nboundaryDuality = layer0[\"BoundaryDuality\"];\n\
temporalMode = layer0[\"TemporalMode\"];\nsubstrate = layer0[\"Substrate\"];\n\
```\n\nBasic verification object:\n\n```wl\nlayer0\n```\n\n## 1.2 Layer L1: \
symbolic field content\n\nThe primary field is a triadic state variable\n$$\n\
\\Psi[\\rho,\\chi,R],\n$$\nwhere:\n\n- $\\rho$ is information density,\n- \
$\\chi$ is field complexity,\n- $R$ is observational resolution.\n\nWe \
implement these as scalar fields over a spatial domain.\n\n```wl\nClearAll[x, \
y, z, \\[CapitalOmega], \\[Rho], \\[Chi], res, coords2D, coords3D];\ncoords2D \
= {x, y};\ncoords3D = {x, y, z};\n```\n\nDefine the L1 action density from \
the supplied variational principle:\n\n$$\n\\mathcal{L}(\\rho,\\chi,R) = \
\\rho\\log(\\chi) + \\chi R^2.\n$$\n\n```wl\nClearAll[actionDensity];\n\
actionDensity[\\[Rho]_, \\[Chi]_, res_] := \\[Rho] Log[\\[Chi]] + \\[Chi] \
res^2;\n```\n\nFor field-theoretic derivations we promote the quantities to \
fields over coordinates:\n\n```wl\nClearAll[\\[Rho]f, \\[Chi]f, resf, \
lagrangian2D, lagrangian3D];\n\nlagrangian2D = actionDensity[\\[Rho]f[x, y], \
\\[Chi]f[x, y], resf[x, y]];\nlagrangian3D = actionDensity[\\[Rho]f[x, y, z], \
\\[Chi]f[x, y, z], resf[x, y, z]];\n```\n\n## 1.3 Layer L2: measured reality\n\
\nMeasured observables are defined as integrated functionals of the Layer L1 \
state over a chosen eigenbasis or domain.\n\n```wl\n\
ClearAll[measurementFunctional];\nmeasurementFunctional[psi_, vars_List, \
region_: Automatic] := \n  If[region === Automatic,\n    Integrate[psi, \
Sequence @@ ({#, -Infinity, Infinity} & /@ vars)],\n    Integrate[psi, \
Element[vars, region]]\n  ];\n```\n\n---\n\n# 2. Variational derivation of \
the L1 field equations\n\n## 2.1 Euler--Lagrange stationarity conditions\n\n\
Because the supplied action density contains no derivatives of the fields, \
the Euler--Lagrange equations reduce to algebraic stationarity conditions:\n\n\
$$\n\\frac{\\partial \\mathcal{L}}{\\partial \\rho} = 0,\n\\qquad\n\
\\frac{\\partial \\mathcal{L}}{\\partial \\chi} = 0,\n\\qquad\n\
\\frac{\\partial \\mathcal{L}}{\\partial R} = 0.\n$$\n\n```wl\n\
ClearAll[stationarityEquations];\nstationarityEquations[\\[Rho]_, \\[Chi]_, \
res_] := Thread[\n   D[actionDensity[\\[Rho], \\[Chi], res], {{\\[Rho], \
\\[Chi], res}}] == 0\n];\n\nelEquations = stationarityEquations[\\[Rho], \
\\[Chi], res]\n```\n\nExpected output:\n\n```wl\n(* {Log[\\[Chi]] == 0, \
\\[Rho]/\\[Chi] + res^2 == 0, 2 \\[Chi] res == 0} *)\n```\n\n## 2.2 Exact \
symbolic solution of the stationarity system\n\n```wl\n\
ClearAll[exactStationarySolutions];\nexactStationarySolutions = \
FullSimplify@Solve[elEquations, {\\[Rho], \\[Chi], res}, Reals]\n```\n\nThis \
derives the exact stationary branch implied by the action.\n\n## 2.3 \
Interpretation of the exact branch\n\nFrom the symbolic system:\n\n- \
$\\log(\\chi)=0$ implies $\\chi=1$,\n- $2\\chi R=0$ then gives $R=0$ because \
$\\chi=1$,\n- $\\rho/\\chi + R^2 = 0$ gives $\\rho=0$.\n\nThus the strict \
stationary point of the stated action is the unique real branch\n$$\n\
(\\rho,\\chi,R)=(0,1,0).\n$$\n\nWe verify this directly:\n\n```wl\n\
stationaryPoint = {\\[Rho] -> 0, \\[Chi] -> 1, res -> 0};\n\
FullSimplify[elEquations /. stationaryPoint]\n```\n\n---\n\n# 3. \
Missing-variable analysis relative to standard physics parameters\n\nThe \
framework requests a comparison between variables in the L1 action and \
standard-model constants.\n\nBecause the action only contains the formal \
symbols $\\rho,\\chi,R$, the complement relative to a chosen list of \
conventional constants is simply the set of OPF variables not identified with \
those constants.\n\n```wl\nClearAll[opfVariables, standardPhysicsSymbols, \
missingVariables];\nopfVariables = {\\[Rho], \\[Chi], res};\n\
standardPhysicsSymbols = {c, \\[HBar], G, kB, e, me, mp};\nmissingVariables = \
Complement[opfVariables, standardPhysicsSymbols]\n```\n\nWe also construct a \
generic solve-always consistency check for the field equations:\n\n```wl\n\
ClearAll[solveAlwaysCheck];\nsolveAlwaysCheck = SolveAlways[\n   And @@ \
(Subtract @@@ elEquations == 0),\n   {\\[Rho], \\[Chi], res}\n]\n```\n\nSince \
the equations are not identities in the variables, this check is expected to \
be restrictive rather than universal.\n\n---\n\n# 4. Local stability and \
spectral analysis\n\n## 4.1 Hessian analysis at the stationary point\n\nFor \
an action density without derivative terms, the local stability is governed \
by the Hessian matrix of second derivatives.\n\n```wl\nClearAll[hessian];\n\
hessian = D[actionDensity[\\[Rho], \\[Chi], res], {{\\[Rho], \\[Chi], res}, \
2}]\n```\n\nEvaluate at the stationary point:\n\n```wl\nhessianAtStationary = \
FullSimplify[hessian /. stationaryPoint]\n```\n\nCompute eigenvalues:\n\n\
```wl\nspectralData = Eigensystem[hessianAtStationary]\n```\n\n## 4.2 \
Interpretation of spectral branches\n\nThe eigenvalues determine whether the \
stationary point is locally minimizing, maximizing, or saddle-like. Any zero \
eigenvalues indicate flat directions in the bare action density.\n\nA test \
summary object:\n\n```wl\nstabilitySummary = <|\n   \"StationaryPoint\" -> \
stationaryPoint,\n   \"Hessian\" -> hessianAtStationary,\n   \"EigenSystem\" \
-> spectralData\n|>;\n```\n\n## 4.3 Linearized maintenance dynamics\n\nThe \
framework specifies a maintenance operator\n$$\n\\frac{d u}{dt} + \\Gamma u = \
0.\n$$\n\nWe solve this exactly for a generic observable mode $u(t)$.\n\n\
```wl\nClearAll[u, t, \\[CapitalGamma], maintenanceEquation, \
maintenanceSolution];\nmaintenanceEquation = u'[t] + \\[CapitalGamma] u[t] == \
0;\nmaintenanceSolution = DSolveValue[{maintenanceEquation, u[0] == u0}, u, \
t]\n```\n\nThis yields\n$$\n u(t) = u_0 e^{-\\Gamma t}.\n$$\n\nUndamped \
harmonic modes require purely imaginary eigenvalues in a second-order or \
Hamiltonian-type system; the first-order maintenance equation instead yields \
exponential decay, neutrality, or growth depending on $\\Re(\\Gamma)$.\n\nWe \
classify these cases symbolically:\n\n```wl\n\
ClearAll[maintenanceClassification];\nmaintenanceClassification = Piecewise[{\
\n   {\"Decay\", Re[\\[CapitalGamma]] > 0},\n   {\"Neutral\", \
Re[\\[CapitalGamma]] == 0},\n   {\"Growth\", Re[\\[CapitalGamma]] < 0}\n}]\n\
```\n\n---\n\n# 5. Residual analysis and formal verification obligations\n\n\
## 5.1 Residuals of the Euler stationarity equations\n\n```wl\n\
ClearAll[residualVector];\nresidualVector[\\[Rho]_, \\[Chi]_, res_] := \n  \
D[actionDensity[\\[Rho], \\[Chi], res], {{\\[Rho], \\[Chi], res}}];\n\n\
residualAtStationary = FullSimplify[residualVector[\\[Rho], \\[Chi], res] /. \
stationaryPoint]\n```\n\nResidual norm:\n\n```wl\nClearAll[residualNorm];\n\
residualNorm[\\[Rho]_, \\[Chi]_, res_] := \
FullSimplify[Norm[residualVector[\\[Rho], \\[Chi], res]]];\n\
residualNormAtStationary = residualNorm[\\[Rho], \\[Chi], res] /. \
stationaryPoint\n```\n\n## 5.2 Exact proof-style verification for the \
stationary branch\n\nWe verify that the derived branch indeed satisfies the \
equations.\n\n```wl\nClearAll[proofCheck];\nproofCheck = FullSimplify[And @@ \
(elEquations /. stationaryPoint)]\n```\n\n## 5.3 Logical implication check\n\n\
```wl\nClearAll[logicalReduction];\nlogicalReduction = Reduce[elEquations, \
{\\[Rho], \\[Chi], res}, Reals]\n```\n\nThis is the rigorous canonical \
representation of all real stationary solutions implied by the action.\n\n---\
\n\n# 6. Domain-regularized field model for nontrivial PDE testing\n\nThe \
supplied action density contains no derivatives and therefore does not \
generate a genuine PDE system. To support verification-first PDE experiments \
while preserving the original stationary content, we introduce a \
**regularized extension** with gradient penalties:\n\n$$\n\
\\mathcal{L}_{\\mathrm{reg}} = \\rho\\log(\\chi) + \\chi R^2 + \
\\frac{\\alpha_\\rho}{2}|\\nabla \\rho|^2 + \\frac{\\alpha_\\chi}{2}|\\nabla \
\\chi|^2 + \\frac{\\alpha_R}{2}|\\nabla R|^2.\n$$\n\nThis section is \
explicitly an **analytic extension for well-posed PDE verification**, not \
part of the bare action unless adopted as an additional axiom.\n\n```wl\n\
ClearAll[\\[Alpha]\\[Rho], \\[Alpha]\\[Chi], \\[Alpha]res, gradSq2D, \
regLagrangian2D];\n\ngradSq2D[f_] := D[f[x, y], x]^2 + D[f[x, y], y]^2;\n\n\
regLagrangian2D = \n  actionDensity[\\[Rho]f[x, y], \\[Chi]f[x, y], resf[x, \
y]] + \n  (\\[Alpha]\\[Rho]/2) gradSq2D[\\[Rho]f] + \n  (\\[Alpha]\\[Chi]/2) \
gradSq2D[\\[Chi]f] + \n  (\\[Alpha]res/2) gradSq2D[resf];\n```\n\nCompute \
formal Euler--Lagrange PDEs:\n\n```wl\nClearAll[eulerLagrange2D];\n\
eulerLagrange2D = {\n  D[regLagrangian2D, \\[Rho]f[x, y]] - \
D[D[regLagrangian2D, D[\\[Rho]f[x, y], x]], x] - D[D[regLagrangian2D, \
D[\\[Rho]f[x, y], y]], y] == 0,\n  D[regLagrangian2D, \\[Chi]f[x, y]] - \
D[D[regLagrangian2D, D[\\[Chi]f[x, y], x]], x] - D[D[regLagrangian2D, \
D[\\[Chi]f[x, y], y]], y] == 0,\n  D[regLagrangian2D, resf[x, y]] - \
D[D[regLagrangian2D, D[resf[x, y], x]], x] - D[D[regLagrangian2D, D[resf[x, \
y], y]], y] == 0\n} // FullSimplify\n```\n\n---\n\n# 7. Exact \
constant-solution verification of the regularized PDEs\n\nThe constant branch \
inherited from the bare action should also solve the regularized PDEs because \
all gradients vanish.\n\n```wl\nClearAll[constantBranch2D];\nconstantBranch2D \
= {\n  \\[Rho]f[x, y] -> 0,\n  \\[Chi]f[x, y] -> 1,\n  resf[x, y] -> 0\n};\n\n\
regularizedConstantCheck = FullSimplify[eulerLagrange2D /. constantBranch2D]\n\
```\n\n---\n\n# 8. Spectral linearization of the regularized PDEs around the \
stationary branch\n\nLet\n$$\n\\rho = 0 + \\epsilon r, \\qquad \\chi = 1 + \
\\epsilon c, \\qquad R = 0 + \\epsilon q.\n$$\n\nWe derive the first-order \
linearized equations.\n\n```wl\nClearAll[\\[Epsilon], r, c, q, linRules, \
linearizedPDEs];\nlinRules = {\n   \\[Rho]f[x, y] -> \\[Epsilon] r[x, y],\n   \
\\[Chi]f[x, y] -> 1 + \\[Epsilon] c[x, y],\n   resf[x, y] -> \\[Epsilon] q[x, \
y]\n};\n\nlinearizedPDEs = Normal@Series[eulerLagrange2D /. linRules, \
{\\[Epsilon], 0, 1}] /. Equal -> Subtract // Expand // Coefficient[#, \
\\[Epsilon], 1] & /@ # &\n```\n\nRecast them as equations:\n\n```wl\n\
linearizedEquations = Thread[linearizedPDEs == 0] // FullSimplify\n```\n\n## \
8.1 Plane-wave spectral substitution\n\nFor local spectral testing, use the \
plane-wave ansatz\n$$\n(r,c,q) \\propto e^{i(k_x x + k_y y)}.\n$$\n\n```wl\n\
ClearAll[kx, ky, rr, cc, qq, planeWaveRules];\nplaneWaveRules = {\n  r[x, y] \
-> rr Exp[I (kx x + ky y)],\n  c[x, y] -> cc Exp[I (kx x + ky y)],\n  q[x, y] \
-> qq Exp[I (kx x + ky y)]\n};\n\nspectralAlgebraicSystem = \n  \
FullSimplify[(linearizedPDEs /. planeWaveRules)/Exp[I (kx x + ky y)]]\n```\n\n\
Build the coefficient matrix:\n\n```wl\nClearAll[spectralMatrix];\n\
spectralMatrix = CoefficientArrays[spectralAlgebraicSystem, {rr, cc, \
qq}][[2]] // Normal\n```\n\nIts determinant gives the dispersion constraint \
for nontrivial modes:\n\n```wl\ndispersionRelation = \
FullSimplify[Det[spectralMatrix]]\n```\n\nEigenvalue-style information:\n\n\
```wl\nspectralEigenvalues = Eigenvalues[spectralMatrix] // FullSimplify\n```\
\n\n---\n\n# 9. Observable construction and measurement kernel\n\nWe now \
define the formal measurement map from L1 fields to observables.\n\n## 9.1 \
General measurement operator\n\n```wl\nClearAll[measurementKernel];\n\
measurementKernel[psi_, vars_List, region_] := Integrate[psi, Element[vars, \
region]];\n```\n\n## 9.2 Example on a bounded disk domain\n\n```wl\n\
ClearAll[diskRegion, psiExample, diskObservable];\ndiskRegion = Disk[{0, 0}, \
a];\npsiExample = \\[Rho]f[x, y] + \\[Chi]f[x, y] + resf[x, y];\n\n\
diskObservable = measurementKernel[psiExample /. constantBranch2D, {x, y}, \
diskRegion] // FullSimplify\n```\n\nSince the constant branch gives $\\Psi = \
1$, this should return the area of the disk.\n\n---\n\n# 10. Composed L0 \.1a \
L1 \.1a L2 morphism pipeline\n\nWe now expose a callable symbolic pipeline \
implementing the three-layer map.\n\n```wl\nClearAll[layer0ToLayer1, \
layer1ToLayer2, opfPipeline];\n\nlayer0ToLayer1[geom_] := <|\n   \"Geometry\" \
-> geom,\n   \"ActionDensity\" -> actionDensity[\\[Rho], \\[Chi], res],\n   \
\"StationarityEquations\" -> stationarityEquations[\\[Rho], \\[Chi], res],\n  \
 \"StationarySolutions\" -> Solve[stationarityEquations[\\[Rho], \\[Chi], \
res], {\\[Rho], \\[Chi], res}, Reals]\n|>;\n\n\
layer1ToLayer2[state_Association, vars_List, region_] := <|\n   \
\"InputState\" -> state,\n   \"Observable\" -> measurementKernel[\n      \
(\\[Rho] + \\[Chi] + res) /. First[state[\"StationarySolutions\"]],\n      \
vars,\n      region\n   ]\n|>;\n\nopfPipeline = RightComposition[\n   \
layer0ToLayer1,\n   layer1ToLayer2[#, {x, y}, Disk[{0, 0}, a]] &\n];\n```\n\n\
Execute the symbolic pipeline:\n\n```wl\nopfPipeline[layer0[\"Geometry\"]]\n\
```\n\n---\n\n# 11. Formal consistency review suite\n\nThis section gathers \
consistency checks in a single structured report.\n\n```wl\n\
ClearAll[consistencyReview];\nconsistencyReview := Dataset@{\n   \
reportTest[\"Layer0 geometry declared\", MatchQ[layer0[\"Geometry\"], \
_Sphere]],\n   reportTest[\"Temporal mode is timeless\", temporalMode === \
\"Timeless\"],\n   reportTest[\"Bare action stationary equations derived\", \
elEquations],\n   reportTest[\"Exact stationary solution exists\", \
exactStationarySolutions],\n   reportTest[\"Stationary point satisfies \
equations\", proofCheck],\n   reportTest[\"Residual vanishes at stationary \
point\", residualNormAtStationary == 0],\n   reportTest[\"Hessian \
available\", MatrixQ[hessianAtStationary]],\n   reportTest[\"Linear \
maintenance solution\", maintenanceSolution],\n   reportTest[\"Regularized \
PDEs derived\", eulerLagrange2D],\n   reportTest[\"Constant branch solves \
regularized PDEs\", regularizedConstantCheck],\n   reportTest[\"Spectral \
matrix computed\", MatrixQ[spectralMatrix]],\n   reportTest[\"Pipeline \
callable\", Head[opfPipeline] =!= Symbol]\n};\n\nconsistencyReview\n```\n\n\
---\n\n# 12. Extended symbolic review passes\n\n## 12.1 Pass A: algebraic \
minimization of the action density\n\n```wl\nClearAll[actionAtStationary, \
actionMinimizationCheck];\nactionAtStationary = actionDensity[\\[Rho], \
\\[Chi], res] /. stationaryPoint;\nactionMinimizationCheck = Reduce[\n   \
actionDensity[\\[Rho], \\[Chi], res] < actionAtStationary,\n   {\\[Rho], \
\\[Chi], res},\n   Reals\n]\n```\n\nThis determines whether the stationary \
point is a strict local or global minimizer. Because the Lagrangian contains \
a logarithm and mixed-sign terms, convexity is not automatic.\n\n## 12.2 Pass \
B: domain restrictions\n\nThe logarithm requires\n$$\n\\chi > 0.\n$$\n\nWe \
explicitly record admissibility:\n\n```wl\nClearAll[admissibilityConditions];\
\nadmissibilityConditions = \\[Chi] > 0;\n```\n\nCombine with stationarity:\n\
\n```wl\nadmissibleSolutionSet = Reduce[elEquations && \
admissibilityConditions, {\\[Rho], \\[Chi], res}, Reals]\n```\n\n## 12.3 Pass \
C: singular perturbation near $\\chi=0$\n\n```wl\nClearAll[singularLimit];\n\
singularLimit = Limit[actionDensity[\\[Rho], \\[Chi], res], \\[Chi] -> 0, \
Direction -> \"FromAbove\"]\n```\n\nThis tests whether the model admits \
finite action near the logarithmic singularity.\n\n## 12.4 Pass D: asymptotic \
growth at large resolution\n\n```wl\nClearAll[largeResolutionLimit];\n\
largeResolutionLimit = Assuming[\\[Chi] > 0, Limit[actionDensity[\\[Rho], \
\\[Chi], res], res -> Infinity]]\n```\n\n---\n\n# 13. Numerical experiments \
with controlled assumptions\n\nThis section is intentionally separated from \
the exact symbolic derivations.\n\n## 13.1 Parameterized regularized energy \
on a square domain\n\n```wl\nClearAll[squareRegion, testFields, \
energyFunctional2D];\nsquareRegion = Rectangle[{-1, -1}, {1, 1}];\n\n\
energyFunctional2D[\\[Rho]Expr_, \\[Chi]Expr_, resExpr_, pars_Association] := \
Integrate[\n   (\n     actionDensity[\\[Rho]Expr, \\[Chi]Expr, resExpr] +\n   \
  (pars[\"AlphaRho\"]/2) (D[\\[Rho]Expr, x]^2 + D[\\[Rho]Expr, y]^2) +\n     \
(pars[\"AlphaChi\"]/2) (D[\\[Chi]Expr, x]^2 + D[\\[Chi]Expr, y]^2) +\n     \
(pars[\"AlphaRes\"]/2) (D[resExpr, x]^2 + D[resExpr, y]^2)\n   ),\n   \
Element[{x, y}, squareRegion],\n   Assumptions -> {pars[\"AlphaRho\"] > 0, \
pars[\"AlphaChi\"] > 0, pars[\"AlphaRes\"] > 0}\n];\n```\n\n## 13.2 \
Trial-family comparison against the constant branch\n\n```wl\n\
ClearAll[trialRho, trialChi, trialRes, trialPars, trialEnergy];\ntrialRho = \
a1 Cos[Pi x] Cos[Pi y];\ntrialChi = 1 + a2 Cos[Pi x] Cos[Pi y];\ntrialRes = \
a3 Cos[Pi x] Cos[Pi y];\n\ntrialPars = <|\"AlphaRho\" -> ar, \"AlphaChi\" -> \
ac, \"AlphaRes\" -> aq|>;\n\ntrialEnergy = FullSimplify[\n   \
energyFunctional2D[trialRho, trialChi, trialRes, trialPars],\n   Assumptions \
-> {ac > 0, ar > 0, aq > 0, -1 < a2 < 1}\n]\n```\n\nCompare with the constant \
branch energy:\n\n```wl\nconstantEnergy = energyFunctional2D[0, 1, 0, \
trialPars] // FullSimplify\n```\n\nEnergy difference:\n\n```wl\n\
energyDifference = FullSimplify[\n   trialEnergy - constantEnergy,\n   \
Assumptions -> {ac > 0, ar > 0, aq > 0, -1 < a2 < 1}\n]\n```\n\n---\n\n# 14. \
Proof and theorem infrastructure for future extensions\n\nThe notebook can \
also be extended with formal proof objects for algebraic consequences.\n\nA \
minimal equational-proof example illustrating the workflow:\n\n```wl\n\
proofExample = FindEquationalProof[\n   ForAll[x, f[g[x]] == g[f[x]]],\n   \
ForAll[x, f[x] == g[x]]\n];\n```\n\nView the proof notebook:\n\n```wl\n\
proofExample[\"ProofNotebook\"]\n```\n\nRelevant functions include \
[FindEquationalProof](paclet:ref/FindEquationalProof), \
[ProofObject](paclet:ref/ProofObject), and \
[AxiomaticTheory](paclet:ref/AxiomaticTheory).\n\n---\n\n# 15. Geometry \
verification infrastructure for the spherical substrate\n\nSince the \
foundational geometric substrate is spherical, one can use symbolic geometry \
tools to construct and test geometric consequences independently of the field \
dynamics.\n\nExample entry points include \
[GeometricScene](paclet:ref/GeometricScene), \
[GeometricAssertion](paclet:ref/GeometricAssertion), \
[GeometricTest](paclet:ref/GeometricTest), and \
[FindGeometricConjectures](paclet:ref/FindGeometricConjectures).\n\nA \
placeholder scene illustrating rigorous geometry tooling:\n\n```wl\n\
ClearAll[geomScene];\ngeomScene = GeometricScene[\n   {p1, p2, p3, p4},\n   {\
\n     CircleThrough[{p1, p2, p3}],\n     GeometricAssertion[\"Concyclic\", \
{p1, p2, p3, p4}]\n   }\n];\n```\n\nThis section is infrastructural and \
deliberately separate from the OPF variational content.\n\n---\n\n# 16. Final \
canonical outputs\n\n## 16.1 Bare-action canonical result\n\nThe strict real \
stationary solution of the supplied action is:\n\n```wl\ncanonicalBareResult \
= <|\n   \"ActionDensity\" -> actionDensity[\\[Rho], \\[Chi], res],\n   \
\"DomainCondition\" -> (\\[Chi] > 0),\n   \"StationaryEquations\" -> \
elEquations,\n   \"RealStationarySolution\" -> stationaryPoint,\n   \
\"ResidualAtSolution\" -> residualAtStationary,\n   \"HessianAtSolution\" -> \
hessianAtStationary,\n   \"EigenvaluesAtSolution\" -> \
Eigenvalues[hessianAtStationary]\n|>;\n\ncanonicalBareResult\n```\n\n## 16.2 \
Regularized-PDE canonical result\n\n```wl\ncanonicalRegularizedResult = <|\n  \
 \"RegularizedLagrangian2D\" -> regLagrangian2D,\n   \"EulerLagrangeEquations\
\" -> eulerLagrange2D,\n   \"ConstantSolutionCheck\" -> \
regularizedConstantCheck,\n   \"LinearizedEquations\" -> linearizedEquations,\
\n   \"SpectralMatrix\" -> spectralMatrix,\n   \"DispersionRelation\" -> \
dispersionRelation\n|>;\n\ncanonicalRegularizedResult\n```\n\n---\n\n# 17. \
Recommended execution order\n\nEvaluate the notebook in the following order:\n\
\n1. Sections 1--5 for exact symbolic derivation of the bare theory.\n2. \
Sections 6--8 for regularized PDE verification.\n3. Sections 9--10 for \
observable construction and pipeline composition.\n4. Sections 11--13 for \
internal review passes and numerical experiments.\n5. Sections 14--15 only if \
formal proof or geometry infrastructure is needed.\n\n---\n\n# 18. Summary\n\n\
Within the formal model stated here, the main rigorous conclusions are:\n\n- \
The supplied bare L1 action density yields **algebraic** Euler stationarity \
conditions, not a nontrivial PDE.\n- Its unique real stationary branch is\n  \
$$\n  (\\rho,\\chi,R) = (0,1,0).\n  $$\n- The maintenance operator yields \
exponential evolution of the form\n  $$\n  u(t)=u_0 e^{-\\Gamma t}.\n  $$\n- \
A genuine PDE system requires additional derivative terms; a regularized \
extension has therefore been introduced explicitly and separately for \
verification studies.\n- All formal checks are organized so that exact \
derivations, consistency checks, numerical experiments, and interpretation \
remain clearly separated.\n\nThis notebook is designed as a rigorous starting \
point for further theorem proving, variational refinement, spectral analysis, \
and controlled numerical testing.\n/exec\nRESULT\n\
